  "premise_review": [
    "Preserve every exact C/F/nabla/Hflow/e/D/H/T/N parameter, all @ explicit argument applications and all three fields. The source package requires typed indexFixedTensor, typed tensorBoundary over exactly indexFixedTensor.fixedPointContract, and a proof of N.nonzeroIndex. No independent bare Prop is selected by this local record.",
    "Full captured NonvanishingIndex source was read: the N used here is the cohomology-contract NonvanishingIndex whose nonzeroIndex is an arbitrary proposition with supplied witness. It is not the distinct NonvanishingWittIndex record with a concrete inequality predicate. No arithmetic/index nonzero formula is inferred from the field name.",
    "The theorem has actual proof content: under the complete supplied B package it concludes AdelicInfinityTopos.AllZerosOnCriticalLine B.tensorBoundary.alignmentContract by exactly B.tensorBoundary.alignmentConclusion. It does not use B.nonzeroIndex, the fixed-tensor implication, or construct any bridge data.",
    "Full captured BoundaryAlignmentBridge source was read: tensorBoundary already requires alignmentConclusion : AllZerosOnCriticalLine alignmentContract, while fixedTensorSuppliesAlignment is a separately supplied arbitrary proposition. The source theorem projects the already assumed actual universal conclusion rather than deriving it from the arbitrary proposition or nonzero index evidence.",
    "Full CriticalLineConclusion/SpectralBoundaryAlignment/LFunctionZero/CriticalLine sources were read. AllZerosOnCriticalLine is a genuine universal statement: for each z in the supplied contract.Zeros, zeroData z has realPart equal to the original symbolic Core.spectralPivot. The definition is not an arbitrary named proposition.",
    "contract.Zeros is an arbitrary Type and may be empty. The source provides no completeness/enumeration relation to actual zeros of a constructed analytic L-function; typed zero labels and realPart fields do not establish such a relation. No Riemann-hypothesis, independent critical-line, analytic or numerical-pivot theorem is claimed.",
    "Full IndexFixedTensorBridge and TensorFixedPointContract contexts were read: actual conditional fixed-tensor existence, horizontal predicates and fixed-section equality proofs are preserved and recognized. Their supplied implications/witnesses are not constructed or applied by this theorem.",
    "The local record is a coherent actual typed conditional package, with no independently chosen bare proposition field. Retain the complete record, original inner namespace and exact theorem as one component; no field dropping, type weakening, new legacy self-import, alias or provider substitution is introduced.",
    "Only outer containing namespaces and explicit Folder/Folder.CrystallineIndex lookup scaffolding change. The exact original imports, every statement/proof byte and inner namespace remain unchanged; historical environment compatibility and Lean elaboration remain unreplayed."
  ],
